endobj
1152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 351 0 R
/T (1. Why use a "Three-Layer AI" approach instead of a single predictive model?)
/E (1. Why use a "Three-Layer AI" approach instead of a single predictive model?)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1153 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 351 0 R
/E (Traditional markets are complex and unpredictable, so relying on time-series data alone isn't enough to reflect real conditions on the ground. Our system therefore combines three approaches: time-series models for forecasting, YOLOv8-based computer vision for visual ground-truth data, and OCR to digitize manual records. This way, predictions are backed not just by historical data, but also by real-world field validation.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1154 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 351 0 R
/T (2. Is this solution scalable to other ASEAN countries?)
/E (2. Is this solution scalable to other ASEAN countries?)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1155 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 351 0 R
/E (Yes, the architecture is highly modular. The YOLOv8 model can be retrained to recognize different local commodities, and the OCR module works broadly since manual record-keeping is common across ASEAN traditional markets. This makes the system well-suited for regional replication under the ASEAN Integrated Food Security \(AIFS\) Framework.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1156 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 351 0 R
/T (3. How do you mitigate the risk of prediction errors)
/E (3. How do you mitigate the risk of prediction errors)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1157 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 351 0 R
/E (Weather-price correlations tend to be weak when applied at a national level. Our model addresses this by calculating correlations per supply source instead of relying on a national average, which prevents errors from being "averaged out." This allows us to generate a more granular Risk Matrix \(Low to Critical\), helping traders take preventive action rather than depend on generic, one-size-fits-all statistics.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1158 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 351 0 R
/T (4. How do you ensure data integrity from inconsistent market sources?)
/E (4. How do you ensure data integrity from inconsistent market sources?)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
